t(8, 610, """A dream published a year ago on the channels: A little girl says to a man: The Mahdi has died and now the look-alike rules us! As for the look-alike, Allah knows best, he is the Qahtani; perhaps by that day he will have gone grey and grown old.

Many people do not understand a long hadith at whose end the Prophet ﷺ says: ((So it will be like that for seven years, or eight years, or nine years; then there is no good in living after him - or he said: then there is no good in life after him)).
Summary of the hadith scholar's ruling: a hasan hadith
Narrator: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri | Reported by Ahmad (3/37) (11344)

The Prophet of Allah Jesus, peace be upon him, will be among the people, and his time is a time of good, of blessing in the fruits, the end of all wars, a completely safe life after Gog and Magog, very high spirituality, and Muslim people turning to worship and to drawing near to Allah the Exalted. This is a context the mind cannot miss: the time of the Prophet of Allah Jesus, peace be upon him, is without doubt a time of good. So why then does the Prophet ﷺ say about the Imam, then there is no good in living after him?

The reason is that most people will have died. People will miss their children, their fathers, their mothers, their brothers, their relatives, their neighbours and those they lived with for years. The time of the Prophet of Allah Jesus, peace be upon him, is among the best of times in terms of the blessing of the earth, and of mixing with a noble prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, and living with him. But the generation among whom the Prophet of Allah Jesus, peace be upon him, will descend is a generation that will have lost its loved ones, whose family, friends, neighbours and relatives have died. Each of them will have no one left of his family, or perhaps one or two persons left of all his family, and Allah knows best. So after the Imam, life has many beauties that did not exist before the Prophet of Allah Jesus, peace be upon him, but in it there is loss and longing for loved ones.""")

t(8, 2290, """The best of times is standing at the door of the King besides whom there is no king .. Stand at His door .. Stand contemplating His beauty .. His mercy .. His gentleness .. His power .. His mighty dominion .. His giving .. His ways in His dominion .. His great favour upon you .. for His favour is great""")

t(9, 690, """Many young men are deceived by false job promises from swindlers' offices, and they take their wives into the unknown. Do not take your wife into the unknown. A young man and his wife in Malaysia in 2024, asking for help .. The young man and his wife sleep in the street, on a bench, sitting up! Young men: think about what you are doing before you take uncalculated steps!""")

t(9, 1625, """The compulsory, overpowering destiny I spoke about before .. I said destiny is of two kinds: the overpowering, in which you are not allowed to take decisions to steer it as you wish .. and the non-overpowering, which you are allowed to steer through means .. In both, the will of our Lord the Most Merciful is present .. stressing that gentleness is part of it .. because Allah the Exalted is All-Aware, Gentle .. Click on the image""")

