t(12, 95, """I visited Sri Lanka, which is very poor in the imagination of many deluded Arabs .. 99% of the people are smiling .. 99% .. Everyone has a home .. Everyone enjoys very excellent infrastructure .. Everyone has the money to buy the ingredients of a dish of vegetables and rice easily, not with great hardship .. They get treatment free .. They study free""")

t(12, 1040, """Date: late 2016 .. Place: Sri Lanka

The incident: A Sri Lankan Muslim was stopped and removed from his seat on a bus, he alone out of all the passengers, so that another, elderly person could sit. The ticket collector scolded the Muslim passenger and spoke to him harshly to make him get up from his seat, while the bus was full of young men of another religion. He got up, helpless, and looked at me with looks that would slay any human being .. looks pleading for help .. I froze in my seat .. I looked down .. I wished the earth would split open and swallow me .. He saw an Arab and wanted to entrust him with a message .. as if he were crying for help to a sleeping world .. a lost world .. a world that has lost its way .. lost its faith .. lost its compass .. And as if he were sending with me a message to all of you .. We are here .. We are the minorities .. we suffer .. we suffer in silence .. Do not be heedless of us .. Do not leave us like this""")

t(12, 2215, """Place: Sri Lanka, very poor in the minds of the Arabs!

The picture: The road between cities! High-quality infrastructure! Infrastructure of which not even 10% exists in the poor Arab countries that boast, in ignorance of history, east and west""")

t(13, 640, """Place: Colombo - Sri Lanka

She wanted to cross the road but was unable to pull the cart .. A Buddhist, not a Muslim .. Muslims came to this world to be a light and a help for every weak person .. That is why we are the best nation brought forth for mankind .. because we were commanded to protect the weak even if he is not a Muslim .. to help the weak even if he is not a Muslim .. to rescue the weak even if he is not a Muslim""")

t(13, 1760, """Place: the Sri Lankan capital Colombo. Date: on one of 7 visits to Sri Lanka .. The incident: A Sri Lankan Muslim man begging on the morning of Eid .. The question: In this world .. why does no one beg on this earth except the Muslims? Why were they deliberately impoverished? In all the non-Muslim countries of the world there is popular support, for understandable reasons, for those of the population who share the majority's religion, and there is an understanding, for known reasons, of why the majority of the population turns away from supporting the Muslim minorities economically .. The Muslim minorities suffer materially .. This is a fact .. They pay the price of the Islamic world's weakness in being denied many of their rights .. This too is a fact .. They pay the price of the existence of an Islamic world that does not hold together, whose parts do not help one another .. Forgotten minorities .. They live in fear at times .. and live in poverty much of the time .. All of these are facts and all of them besiege us .. besiege our consciences .. drive sleep from our eyes .. exhaust us .. and place us all before our responsibilities""")

t(14, 340, """Location: Wadi al-Muluk district in 6th of October City .. Date: late 2024

The story: A woman 60 years of age .. weeping .. praying a great deal .. asking for money to buy her medicine .. her eyes filled with tears! Despite her 60 years, her face shines with beauty and innocence .. purity of heart and cleanness .. I wonder, how did you buy your medicine after we met? O Allah, relieve her distress and the distress of the poor of the Islamic world""")

t(14, 1380, """The rural town: Kalba .. Country: the Emirates .. Date: 1990

Comment on the experience: A person's upbringing in a village is not like his upbringing in a city .. Those raised in villages are more naive .. with less experience of life .. They crawl as children crawl in understanding people's natures .. They will err a lot in understanding life's twists, its hidden sides and its patterns .. and they will pay heavy prices, because the village is safety, yes, and peace and protection .. but it is an abduction from experience .. and an isolation far from the movement of the cities and the clamour of the minds in them!""")

t(14, 2415, """From screams stifled beneath the earth .. coming from another dimension .. travelling on with every century that has passed over mankind .. Your last scream is coming .. because the sands will advance .. and because the earth will split open .. and because the light above you will wear you down .. then in the end .. it will melt you""")

